>> title: Roasted Cauliflower, Air Fryer
>> category: Vegetables & Sides
>> tags: cauliflower, air fryer, basket, side, cumin
>> counters: The Air Fryer & the Pot
>> dish: roasted-cauliflower
>> kit: Air Fryer
>> aka: air fryer cauliflower, basket cauliflower, air fried cauliflower, roasted cauliflower florets
>> servings: 4
>> time: 30 min
>> slack: forgiving — a floret that is not brown yet goes back for three minutes; the steam that pools under it on a tray has somewhere to go here
>> washing-up: the basket, the bowl
>> keeps: not at all — it weeps and softens overnight, and a second pass only dries out what is left

>> step: Written for a preheated 5.7 L basket. From cold, add three minutes. A 3.5 L basket is two batches, not more minutes.
Florets, not slabs. A slab stands up in a basket and blocks the fan.

>> step: cut into even florets, toss with equal parts water and oil
Cut @cauliflower{1%small head}(600 g; leaves off) into even florets and toss in a #bowl{} with @olive oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @water{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @kosher salt{1%tsp}.

>> step: roast in the basket 175°C (350°F), 12–18 min, one layer
Roast @&(~1)wetted florets{} in a preheated #air fryer basket{} at 175°C (350°F) for ~air fry{15%min}, one layer.

>> step: toss the basket at halfway — a loose rattle, cut faces browning
Toss @&(~1)cauliflower{} by shaking the basket once.

>> step: toss hot in the same bowl
Toss @&(~1)roasted cauliflower{} with @lemon{1/2}(juiced), @parsley{2%Tbs}(chopped), @black pepper{1/2%tsp}.

>> step: No test kitchen has published a cauliflower number. This is the broccoli method run longer, because a floret is denser.
The range is the honest answer. Take the middle and read the cut faces.
